sources:
  - title: "Modular proof draft for a planar Schiffer counterexample"
    authors:
      - "Jaume de Dios Pont"
      - "OpenAI Codex"
    id: >-
      https://github.com/caolab97/Schiffer/blob/85235fb037cbfd336e3ae9801f61951c5e2d1c4f/Schiffer_GPT_V3.tex
    type: "original proof manuscript"
    license: "UNLICENSED"
    author_contacted: "n/a"
    prior_work: >-
      The construction adapts cone bifurcation ideas and analytic techniques
      from Fall--Minlend--Weth, The Schiffer problem on the cylinder and on the
      2-sphere; Enciso--Fernandez--Ruiz--Sicbaldi, A Schiffer-type problem for
      annuli; and Cao-Labora--Fernandez, A contractible Schiffer counterexample
      on the half-sphere. The Euclidean large-N landing argument and the final
      counterexample proof were developed in this project.
status:
  scope: >-
    A complete large-N construction of a bounded, star-shaped and simply
    connected planar Schiffer domain that is not a Euclidean disk. The project
    formalizes the weighted Fourier and anisotropic Banach-space foundations,
    the Bessel-function and zero-density spine, a reusable quantitative
    Lyapunov--Schmidt/parametric-contraction reduction, uniform nonlinear cone
    branches, the negative quadratic radius drift, near-integer crossings,
    integer landing, direct Cartesian regularity at the cone tip, one-sided C2
    gluing, and graph/field nontriviality. It also proves a construction-free
    comparator statement with a global C2 defining function and global C2
    field satisfying -Delta u = u, u = 1, and full derivative Du = 0 on the
    boundary. Counts and claims here refer to Schiffer and Schiffer.lean on
    this repository's `lean` branch; legacy Schiffer files and
    the N=28 numerical experiments are outside the formalized proof scope.
  sorry_count: 3
  sorry_in_definitions: 0
  axioms:
    - "propext"
    - "Quot.sound"
    - "Classical.choice"
  notes: >-
    A full default `lake build` completed successfully (3177 jobs). The imported solution
    proof has no sorry or admit. The three sorries counted above occur only in
    the deliberately incomplete pedagogical files `Schiffer/Challenge.lean`
    and `Schiffer/FormalConjecturesChallenge.lean`; neither is imported by
    the solution entry point. Source scans found no custom axiom, unsafe
    declaration, or heartbeat override in the proof. Lean axiom checks and
    LSP source scans were run on the final theorem and the load-bearing branch,
    density, landing, lift, and origin-series declarations.
  main_results:
    - declaration: "Schiffer.Analysis.SchifferCounterexample.PlanarSchifferCounterexample"
      file: "Schiffer/Analysis/SchifferCounterexample.lean"
      sorry_count: 0
      axioms:
        - "propext"
        - "Quot.sound"
        - "Classical.choice"
      literature_dependencies: []
    - declaration: "Schiffer.exists_schifferCounterexample"
      file: "Schiffer/Main.lean"
      sorry_count: 0
      axioms:
        - "propext"
        - "Quot.sound"
        - "Classical.choice"
      literature_dependencies: []
    - declaration: "Schiffer.Bifurcation.exists_uniformConeBranch"
      file: "Schiffer/Bifurcation/UniformBranch.lean"
      sorry_count: 0
      axioms:
        - "propext"
        - "Quot.sound"
        - "Classical.choice"
      literature_dependencies: []
    - declaration: "Schiffer.Density.exists_nearIntegerCrossing"
      file: "Schiffer/Density/NearInteger.lean"
      sorry_count: 0
      axioms:
        - "propext"
        - "Quot.sound"
        - "Classical.choice"
      literature_dependencies: []
    - declaration: "Schiffer.Landing.exists_landedConeSolution"
      file: "Schiffer/Landing/IntegerRadius.lean"
      sorry_count: 0
      axioms:
